// ║   THIS IS THE PERMANENT STANDARD.                                                   ║
// ║                                                                                      ║
// ║   Every time ANY engine updates, it MUST:                                           ║
// ║   1. Check against ALL 7 scale laws (micro → macro)                                 ║
// ║   2. Verify it has MULTIPLE responsibilities (not single-purpose)                   ║
// ║   3. Confirm connections to at least 3 other engine categories                      ║
// ║   4. Validate state against all Medina constants                                    ║
// ║   5. Report to the spherical web                                                    ║
// ║                                                                                      ║
// ║   THE 7 SCALE LAWS (Micro → Macro):                                                 ║
// ║   ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────║
// ║   Scale 1: QUANTUM      — Entanglement, superposition, coherence                    ║
// ║   Scale 2: SYNAPTIC     — Hebbian weights, plasticity, LTP/LTD                     ║
// ║   Scale 3: NEURAL       — Kuramoto sync, oscillation, firing patterns              ║
// ║   Scale 4: CIRCUIT      — Shell integration, pathway activation                     ║
// ║   Scale 5: REGIONAL     — Animal engine coordination, module coupling              ║
// ║   Scale 6: ORGANISM     — Whole-system coherence, OMNIS, heartbeat                 ║
// ║   Scale 7: ECOSYSTEM    — World body, biomes, economic metabolism                  ║
// ║                                                                                      ║
// ║   THE 12 ENGINE CATEGORIES (must connect to 3+):                                    ║
// ║   ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────║
// ║   1. ANIMAL      — Bee, Dolphin, Crow, Elephant, Wolf, etc.                        ║
// ║   2. QUANTUM     — Entanglement, channels, coherence                               ║
// ║   3. NEURAL      — Kuramoto, Hebbian, plasticity                                   ║
// ║   4. COGNITIVE   — Shells, attention, memory                                       ║
// ║   5. ECONOMIC    — FORMA, metals, metabolism                                       ║
// ║   6. TERRITORIAL — Biomes, world body, territory                                   ║
// ║   7. DEFENSE     — VAEL, AEGIS, threats                                            ║
// ║   8. TEMPORAL    — CHRONOS, time scales, episodic                                  ║
// ║   9. SOCIAL      — Swarm, coordination, communication                              ║
// ║   10. CREATIVE   — Dream, synthesis, generation                                    ║
// ║   11. GOVERNANCE — Laws, heartbeat, sovereignty                                    ║
// ║   12. PHYSICAL   — Drones, avatars, real-world                                     ║
// ║                                                                                      ║
